{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791585771,"nonce":"MCaX/ryV7cR987hgsBpczJtKpDA=","message":"Root cause found. Not cross-program pollution: ANY program that loads rayzor.concurrent.Arc from a warm stdlib BLADE cache (and has no .mir.cache of its own) fails. The \"self-warm passes\" observation was the program's own .mir.cache skipping lowering.\n\nregister_method_from_blade reuses an existing method symbol (found by qualified name) and set its scope_id + scope_tree entry, but never indexed it in SymbolTable::symbols_by_name under the new class scope. lookup_symbol(class_scope, \"strongCount\") then missed, the @:autoDeref check decided the method was not on Arc, and rewrote `a.m()` to `a.get().m()`; for `get` itself that rewrite recursed until the compiler stack overflowed (test_channel_*: SIGSEGV), and elsewhere it bound Arc methods to the payload class (Box.strongCount trap stub).\n\nFix: SymbolTable::place_symbol_in_scope for restored methods; the deref rewrite never applies to `get`.\n\nAlso: run_haxe_tests.sh cleared .rayzor/blade/cache/*.blade and .rayzor/cache/*.mir.cache, but the MIR caches and stdlib BLADEs live in .rayzor/blade/cache/*.mir.cache and .rayzor/blade/cache/native/. Stale caches survived between suite runs, which is why the count moved run to run.\n\nRepro: rm -rf .rayzor; rayzor run T.hx; rm .rayzor/blade/cache/*.mir.cache; rayzor run T.hx  (T = new Arc(new Box(5)); a.strongCount()).","files":null}]}